        'Herd mentality was the accelerant. Taxi drivers, hairdressers, and college students were giving stock tips. Not investing in tech felt like missing out. The sunk cost fallacy kept people holding as stocks fell 50%, 70%, 90%, "I can\'t sell now, I\'ve already lost so much." Pets.com, Webvan, and hundreds of companies went to zero. The NASDAQ fell 78% from peak to trough, from 5,048 to 1,114, and took 15 years to recover.'
