        { term: 'Sunk Cost Fallacy', definition: 'Continuing a behavior or investment because of previously invested resources (money, time, effort) rather than future expected returns.', example: 'Holding a stock down 80% because "I\'ve already lost so much, I can\'t sell now", the money is gone regardless of whether you sell or hold.' }
