      'Richard Thaler won the Nobel Prize for proving that people treat money differently based on arbitrary mental labels. A $1,000 tax refund gets spent freely, but earning $1,000 overtime feels \'hard-earned\' and gets saved, even though it\'s the same $1,000.',
      'By the end of this lesson, you\'ll understand mental accounting, framing effects, the sunk cost fallacy, the house money effect, the endowment effect, status quo bias, default bias, and the pain of paying, and how each one silently drains your wealth.',
      'Comparison of how the same $1,000 is treated differently depending on its mental label: tax refund (spent freely) vs overtime pay (saved carefully)',
