            { label: 'Explain the certainty effect: their desire to "lock in" the partial recovery reflects Prospect Theory\'s prediction that people overvalue certainty. Show them historical recovery data and reaffirm the long-term plan', consequence: 'Excellent. The couple is exhibiting the certainty effect, the certain "smaller loss" feels emotionally superior to the uncertain "possible full recovery," even though historical data shows that 35% market drops have recovered fully within 1-3 years in virtually every case. Educating them about the specific bias they\'re experiencing, while showing data, empowers rational decision-making.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Ignore their request and do nothing without explanation', consequence: 'Ignoring client concerns damages trust. The couple needs to understand WHY their instinct is counterproductive, not just be overruled. Explaining Prospect Theory gives them a framework to understand their own emotions and builds confidence in the long-term plan.', score: 1 }
