      'Not quite. A nudge must meet three criteria: (1) it predictably changes behavior, (2) it doesn\'t forbid any options, and (3) the economic incentives don\'t significantly change. Auto-enrollment meets all three, participation rises dramatically, but every employee retains the freedom to opt out. This is libertarian paternalism in action.'
