      'Auto-enrolling at 6% (match-maximizing default), implementing SMarT auto-escalation to 15%, creating tiered choice architecture with target-date default, and framing retirement readiness as projected monthly income, scoring 12/12.',
      'Nudge theory transforms the gap between intention and action by redesigning the choice environment rather than trying to change people. The key principle: there is no neutral design, someone must choose the defaults, ordering, and framing. Since design is inevitable, it should be designed to help. Auto-enrollment, SMarT escalation, curated defaults, and personalized framing are the four pillars of effective financial choice architecture. Together, they have added hundreds of billions of dollars to retirement savings worldwide, without removing a single option or forcing a single decision.'
