        'Annie Duke, former professional poker player and author of "Thinking in Bets," argues that judging decisions by outcomes is the most dangerous cognitive error in investing. A bad process can produce a good outcome by luck, while a good process can produce a bad outcome by bad luck. The decision journal forces you to evaluate your PROCESS over time. After 50+ entries, patterns emerge: "I consistently overestimate growth rates" or "I trade more during volatile weeks" or "My best decisions come after consulting my checklist."',
        'The accountability partner is the final component of the rational framework. Research shows that people who publicly commit to a goal are 65% more likely to achieve it. An accountability partner, a trusted friend, advisor, or investing group, reviews your IPS, questions your reasoning, and calls out biases you can\'t see yourself. Charlie Munger serves as Warren Buffett\'s accountability partner: "Charlie has talked me out of more bad investments than anyone." The key: choose someone who will challenge you, not someone who will agree with you.'
