            { label: 'Create a written pre-decision checklist (inspired by Gawande and Pabrai) that must be completed before EVERY trade: thesis review, disconfirming evidence check, emotional state assessment, bias identification, "fresh money" test, and cooling-off period compliance', consequence: 'Excellent. A written checklist forces System 2 engagement by requiring specific analytical steps that can\'t be skipped. Key items: "Have I actively sought disconfirming evidence?" "What is my emotional state on a 1-10 scale?" "Would I buy/sell this at today\'s price with fresh money?" "Am I within my IPS rebalancing triggers?" The checklist is the gatekeeper that prevents emotional trades from reaching execution.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Just automate everything and never think about investing', consequence: 'Full automation (index fund DCA) is actually an excellent strategy for the core portfolio, it eliminates 100% of behavioral biases for the automated portion. But it still requires initial framework design (allocation, contribution rate, rebalancing rules) and the discipline not to override the automation during emotional moments. Automation is a tool WITHIN the framework, not a replacement for it.', score: 1 }
