      'This is the fundamental distinction between process quality and outcome quality. A rational framework doesn\'t eliminate risk, it eliminates BEHAVIORAL errors. An unforeseeable global event is precisely the kind of risk that cannot be avoided, only sized appropriately (which the IPS should ensure). The decision journal will show that the process was sound. Over hundreds of decisions, a good process with occasional bad luck will dramatically outperform a bad process with occasional good luck. Abandoning the framework after one bad outcome would itself be a behavioral error: "resulting."'
