          explanation: 'Think of it this way: if you hold a stock worth $6,000 that you paid $10,000 for, you effectively have $6,000 in cash invested in that stock. Would you buy $6,000 of that stock today? If not, you\'re using sunk cost reasoning to destroy future wealth.'
