          explanation: 'Survivorship bias makes us think stocks always recover because we only remember the ones that did. We forget the thousands of stocks that fell and never came back. Holding a deteriorating business "waiting for recovery" is betting on survivorship bias against the base rate of permanent capital impairment.'
