          explanation: 'The sunk cost version of averaging down: "I paid $100, now it\'s $60, so I\'ll buy more to lower my average to $80." This doesn\'t change the stock\'s intrinsic value, it just increases your concentrated risk. The rational version: "My DCF analysis values this at $90, and at $60 it\'s even more undervalued, so I\'ll increase my position based on forward-looking analysis."'
