            { label: 'Sell at $8,000. The $7,000 loss is a sunk cost. Your research says fair value is $5,000, so you\'re actually selling $3,000 ABOVE intrinsic value. Redeploy the $8,000 to a better opportunity and harvest the $7,000 tax loss to offset gains elsewhere.', consequence: 'Excellent. You identified the sunk cost, applied the clean slate test (you wouldn\'t buy this stock today), recognized you\'re selling above fair value, and captured the tax loss benefit. The $8,000 can now earn returns in a growing investment instead of declining in a shrinking one.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Average down to lower cost basis', consequence: 'You\'d be increasing exposure to a declining business with $5,000 fair value because of the $15,000 you already lost. This is sunk cost escalation, the Concorde pattern at the portfolio level.', score: 0 }
