      'Three years of regret-aversion paralysis at 1% vs 10% returns has already cost ~$33,100 in foregone compound returns. The fear of one bad outcome (buying before a crash) has guaranteed a bad outcome (3 years of inflation erosion). This is the omission bias at work: inaction feels safe but is mathematically worse.'
