            { label: 'Invest the full $30,000 immediately. Markets hit all-time highs regularly, it\'s a sign of a functioning market, not a warning signal. Schwab\'s study proves immediate investing outperforms waiting 67% of the time. If you can\'t invest the lump sum due to regret aversion, use DCA over 3-6 months maximum, but set it up TODAY with automatic transfers.', consequence: 'Excellent. You recognized that all-time highs are normal (not danger signals), cited the Schwab evidence, and took immediate action. You also provided a DCA alternative as a concession to emotional comfort, which is valid as long as the timeframe is short (3-6 months) and automated to prevent further paralysis.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Invest in bonds instead, they\'re safer than stocks right now', consequence: 'This is regret aversion disguised as asset allocation. If your time horizon is 10+ years, bonds historically underperform stocks by 4-6% annually. Choosing bonds because you fear stock market regret sacrifices long-term returns for short-term emotional comfort.', score: 1 }
