            { label: 'Ask a financial advisor to choose for you', consequence: 'Outsourcing the decision can work, but a financial advisor charging 1% annually costs $1,000/year on $100K, far more than the 0.04% difference between funds. If using an advisor breaks paralysis, it has value. But for a simple index fund choice, it\'s using a sledgehammer to crack a nut.', score: 1 }
