            { label: 'Reframe the regret: you\'re experiencing hindsight bias (it feels like you "should have known" the market would drop). Nobody predicted this. Even if you\'d waited 6 months, you would have faced the same fear at a different price. HOLD your position, the 8% drop is noise in a 20-year investment horizon. Review your IPS to confirm your plan hasn\'t changed.', consequence: 'Excellent emotional regulation. You identified the hindsight bias creating false "I should have known" regret, recognized that 8% drops are routine in equity investing (they happen almost every year), and maintained discipline by reviewing your IPS. Over your 20+ year horizon, this 8% dip will be invisible.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Invest more money to average down while prices are low', consequence: 'Adding money during a dip can be rational if it\'s part of your regular investment schedule. But if you\'re adding specifically to "fix" the regret, you\'re being driven by emotion rather than plan. The best approach is to continue your pre-committed investment schedule unchanged, don\'t invest more because of the dip, and don\'t invest less.', score: 1 }
