            { label: 'Keep everything, it\'s worked fine for 8 years', consequence: 'Status quo bias masquerading as satisfaction. You\'re forfeiting 2% employer match ($1,000+/year on a $50K salary). An 8-year-old fund selection may no longer match your risk profile. No auto-escalation means you\'ll be at 4% until you actively change it, which status quo bias makes unlikely.', score: 0 },
            { label: 'Increase contribution to 6% (capture full match), switch to age-appropriate target-date fund, enable auto-escalation at 1%/year up to 15%. Schedule annual review.', consequence: 'Comprehensive default override. Capturing the full match adds ~$1,000+/year in free money. The target-date fund automatically adjusts risk as you age. Auto-escalation will compound your savings dramatically. One 30-minute session changes your retirement trajectory by $200,000+.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Just increase to 6% to capture the match, keep the same fund', consequence: 'Capturing the match is the highest priority and you got that right. But keeping an 8-year-old fund selection and not enabling auto-escalation leaves two status quo traps active. Partial override is better than none, but you\'re still leaving significant money on the table.', score: 1 }
