      'Maximizing 401(k) defaults (contribution, fund, auto-escalation), evaluating advisor fees objectively against the loyalty penalty, and overcoming savings account inertia to capture $840+/year, scoring 9/9.',
      'Status quo bias is the most expensive invisible bias because it operates through INACTION. You don\'t feel the cost because you never made a "bad decision", you simply didn\'t make a good one. The antidote is the default audit: systematically evaluate every financial setting, not when you feel like it, but on a scheduled annual basis. The 2-3 hours spent on a default audit can unlock $5,000-$50,000+ per year in captured employer matching, reduced fees, higher interest, and better fund selection. Make the optimal choice the lazy choice, and let inertia build your wealth instead of destroying it.'
