      'After every market move, CNBC provides a compelling explanation: "Stocks fell on inflation fears" or "Markets rallied on strong earnings." But a 2019 study found that identical market movements on different days received completely opposite explanations, proving the narratives are created AFTER the fact to explain noise.',
      'By the end of this lesson, you\'ll understand why your brain craves stories over statistics, how financial media manufactures narratives from random market noise, and why the most profitable investors ignore the story and follow the data.',
      'Split panel showing identical 2% market drops with contradictory CNBC headlines on different days',
