        { term: 'Narrative Contrarian', definition: 'An investor who systematically positions against the dominant market narrative, buying when the consensus story is bearish and selling when it\'s euphoric. Based on the principle that universal narratives create maximum mispricing.', example: 'Buying stocks in March 2009 when the narrative was "financial system collapse" and selling in late 2021 when the narrative was "stocks only go up."' }
