      'WeWork is the definitive narrative fallacy case study. A simple business (subletting offices) was wrapped in a compelling narrative (technology platform, community, consciousness) that inflated its valuation by 5-10x beyond what fundamentals supported. The S-1 filing, which revealed the data behind the story for the first time, triggered an 83% collapse in weeks. The lesson: narratives can sustain irrational valuations for years, but data always wins eventually. The more compelling the story, the more important it is to check the numbers.'
