            { label: 'Trust your screen. It excluded this stock for a reason: 80x revenue with no earnings is not an investment, it\'s a speculative attention bet. The media coverage, Reddit hype, and friend\'s gain are all attention triggers designed to override rational analysis. Your screen protects you from exactly this scenario.', consequence: 'Disciplined attention resistance. Your screen\'s exclusion of 80x revenue stocks is a rule-based defense against narrative-driven overvaluation. Every attention trigger, media, social proof, FOMO, is working to override your systematic process. Trusting the screen over the noise is how attention-resistant investors preserve capital and outperform.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Buy a small position, you don\'t want to miss out entirely', consequence: 'The "small position" compromise is attention bias negotiating with your rational process. Any amount invested in a stock your screen excluded is a concession to attention over fundamentals. The size doesn\'t matter, the principle does. Your screen has criteria for a reason.', score: 1 }
