            { label: 'Maintain your process. Six months is not a valid evaluation period. The neglected firm effect and value premium play out over years, not months. Your friends\' attention-driven gains are likely temporary, Barber & Odean predict mean reversion. Social pressure from friends is just another form of attention bias. Review in 3+ years.', consequence: 'Maximum discipline. You recognized that 6 months is insufficient to evaluate a fundamental strategy, that peer pressure is a social form of attention bias, and that the research supports your approach over the long term. Lakonishok found that boring value stocks outperform glamour stocks over 5-year periods by 10-11% annually. Short-term underperformance is the price of long-term outperformance.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Move half your portfolio into AI stocks to balance boring and exciting holdings', consequence: 'This is attention bias winning through compromise. Adding attention-driven stocks to a fundamentally-driven portfolio dilutes the return advantage your screen provides. The research is clear: over 3-5 year periods, neglected value stocks outperform attention-driven glamour stocks significantly.', score: 1 }
