      'Investigating the neglected water treatment company, trusting your screen over media hype for the AI stock, and maintaining process discipline despite social pressure, scoring 9/9.',
      'Attention bias is the gateway drug to every other investing mistake. It determines which stocks enter your consideration set, which means it determines everything that follows. If your "investment universe" is defined by CNBC, Reddit, and social gatherings, you\'re competing for the same overpriced stocks as millions of other attention-driven investors. The 1-2% underperformance from attention-driven buying compounds to enormous wealth destruction over decades. The antidote is systematic: build screens, limit news consumption, and accept that the most profitable investments are usually the ones nobody is talking about.'
