            { label: 'Hold, record earnings, 35% growth, and market expansion are strengthening fundamentals. The 120% gain is irrelevant to forward returns. If you\'d buy this stock today at today\'s price with these fundamentals, holding is the correct decision. The thesis is strengthening, not completing.', consequence: 'Perfect. You evaluated forward fundamentals, not backward gains. The 120% tells you nothing about the next 120%. Record earnings and 35% growth suggest the best may be ahead. This is how wealth-creating positions are held through their compounding phase.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Sell half and hold half as a compromise', consequence: 'The compromise is still driven by the gain percentage, not fundamentals. If the thesis supports holding, it supports holding the full position. Selling half captures disposition-effect pressure into a transaction.', score: 1 }
