            { label: 'Sell immediately. Three missed earnings, CEO departure, and losing market share constitute thesis invalidation. Your purchase price is irrelevant. This capital is better deployed in a position with intact fundamentals. Harvest the tax loss to offset gains from winners.', consequence: 'Excellent disposition-effect resistance. You recognized that the loss is real regardless of whether you sell, that the thesis is broken, and that holding is opportunity cost. Harvesting the tax loss adds value by offsetting capital gains. This is exactly what Odean\'s research shows investors should do but rarely do.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Average down, buy more at the lower price to reduce your average cost', consequence: 'Averaging down into a broken thesis is doubling the disposition effect error. You\'re adding capital to a deteriorating position to manipulate your reference point (average cost), which is pure mental accounting. Three consecutive missed earnings is a sell signal, not a buy signal.', score: 0 }
