            { label: 'Sell the losing positions to harvest $12,000 in tax losses, offsetting most of your $15,000 in realized gains. This saves thousands in capital gains taxes. If you still believe in the thesis, repurchase after the 30-day wash sale period. Tax-loss harvesting is the rational response that the disposition effect prevents.', consequence: 'Optimal tax management that directly counters the disposition effect. By realizing losses to offset gains, you save thousands in taxes while redeploying capital efficiently. This is exactly what Odean\'s research shows investors should do, sell losers and defer selling winners, but the disposition effect causes the opposite behavior.', score: 3 }
